meta {
  name: Batch Create Physical Sessions
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/physical/courses/{{physicalCourseId}}/sessions/batch
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "fromDate": "2026-09-01",
    "toDate": "2026-09-30"
  }
}

docs {
  US-PHYSICAL-006 escenario 2. Requires an ADMIN or INSTRUCTOR bearer token
  and an existing `physicalCourseId`.

  Generates one session per date in [fromDate, toDate] that falls on the
  course's recurring day of week, at its startTime and capacity. No holiday
  exclusion — the project has no holidays concept yet.

  Everything is UTC (ADR-0048, #729): `fromDate` and `toDate` are UTC dates, and
  the course's `dayOfWeek` and `startTime` are UTC too. A session is generated
  for each UTC date whose UTC weekday equals the course's `dayOfWeek`, at
  `date + startTime` (UTC). The management client converts the local range to
  UTC dates.

  Todo o nada (#743): si el curso ya tiene una sesión (en cualquier estado, una
  cancelada cuenta) en alguno de los instantes a generar, responde `409
  SESSION_ALREADY_EXISTS` con las fechas repetidas en `conflictingDates` y no
  crea ninguna sesión, tampoco las libres. Ejemplo, al repetir este request
  sobre un curso de los martes UTC:

    {
      "type": "https://menta.dance/problems/session_already_exists",
      "title": "Conflict",
      "status": 409,
      "detail": "The course already has a session at one or more of the requested dates.",
      "code": "SESSION_ALREADY_EXISTS",
      "conflictingDates": ["2026-09-01T23:00:00Z", "2026-09-08T23:00:00Z"]
    }

  Un rango invertido (`fromDate` posterior a `toDate`) o sin ninguna fecha del día
  de la semana del curso responde `400 INVALID_REQUEST` en lugar de `201` con una
  lista vacía:

    {
      "type": "https://menta.dance/problems/invalid_request",
      "title": "Bad Request",
      "status": 400,
      "detail": "The range must have fromDate not after toDate and include a date on the course's day of week.",
      "code": "INVALID_REQUEST"
    }

  Success contract: 201 with PhysicalSessionManagementListResponse.
  Error contract:
    400 INVALID_REQUEST        → inverted range or no date on the course's weekday
    409 SESSION_ALREADY_EXISTS → a session already exists at a generated instant
    403 COURSE_NOT_OWNED → INSTRUCTOR is not the course's professor
    404 COURSE_NOT_FOUND → courseId does not exist
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}
